# Working output. Raw and unsanitised by design: it is where a real value lands
# if one is ever printed. It never gets versioned.
.runs/
exchange/

# Build products. The bundle is produced by the release pipeline from MANIFEST,
# not committed -- a committed bundle is one nobody can prove came from the tag.
*.skill
build/
verify/
__pycache__/

# The process behind the method, not the method: adversarial review briefs and the
# reports they produced. They are working material -- written in Spanish, addressed
# to one person, full of half-formed findings and superseded numbers -- and a reader
# who lands on them mistakes them for documentation of the skill.
#
# They stay on disk. Nothing here is deleted, and the next round still reads them.
# The pattern is `docs-*` and not `docs-review-*`, because the second one was written
# against the files that existed at the time and the next three were called something
# else. A list written from what is in front of you measures what was in front of you.
docs-*

article-*.md
prompt-*.md
